# Reasoned exceptions to scripts/private_material_scan.py.
#
#   <path>:<RULE>:<reason>
#
# A line here is a statement that the occurrence is deliberate and publishable.
# It is not a way to make the scanner quiet. Every entry names a reason, and a
# reason that is only "it was already there" is not one.

# --- the retired product name, where it cannot be removed ---------------------
# sqlx validates a checksum per applied migration, so editing one byte of an
# applied migration stops the server booting against an existing database. Both
# NOTICE files explain this, name these six files, and are the reason the name
# survives at all.
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0002_ledger.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0002_ledger.sql:LAB_VOCAB:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0006_retrieval.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0010_identity_interactions.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0015_storage_backend_vocab.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0016_interactions_instance.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE
server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/0019_authoring_drafts.sql:LEGACY_NAMES:checksummed migration; see NOTICE

# The NOTICE files are where the residue above is explained. They have to be
# able to say the name in order to explain it. The two under server/src are
# byte-identical copies of server/NOTICE, carried inside those crates because a
# published crate cannot reach the file at the repository root.
NOTICE:LEGACY_NAMES:explains the migration residue it names
server/NOTICE:LEGACY_NAMES:explains the migration residue it names
server/src/munarium-api-types/NOTICE:LEGACY_NAMES:byte-identical copy of server/NOTICE, packaged with the crate
server/src/munarium-proto/NOTICE:LEGACY_NAMES:byte-identical copy of server/NOTICE, packaged with the crate

# The clients' notices file reproduces each component's own NOTICE verbatim,
# and two of its components are the server crates above. Their NOTICE is the
# one that explains the residue, so the same text lands here, and the same
# reason covers it. Regenerated by clients/third_party_notices.py; not edited.
clients/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:LEGACY_NAMES:reproduces the NOTICE of munarium-api-types and munarium-proto, whose exception is above

# --- the scanner itself -------------------------------------------------------
# It holds the patterns, so it matches all of them.
scripts/private_material_scan.py:LEGACY_NAMES:the rule definitions
scripts/private_material_scan.py:LAB_VOCAB:the rule definitions
scripts/private_material_scan.py:PRIVATE_PLANS:the rule definitions
scripts/private_material_scan.py:PRIVATE_CORPORA:the rule definitions
scripts/private_material_scan.py:MEASUREMENTS:the rule definitions
scripts/private_material_scan.py:LIVE_ENV_VARS:the rule definitions

# --- generated screenshots ----------------------------------------------------
# These are not diagrams: they are screenshots of the operator console, produced
# by matrix/ui-smoke/smoke.mjs against a live compose stack. Their source is the
# generator and the console itself, so there is no .svg to sit beside them, and
# hand-editing one would make it a drawing of a UI rather than a picture of it.
# Regenerate with `matrix/test.ps1 -BlackBox -Browser` before a release; the
# current set was captured on 2026-09-04 against Matrix 1.0.0, contract 0.1.0
# and Server 1.0.0 in exact lockstep.
